        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: The common denominator for \\(\\frac{C}{x-3} + \\frac{D}{x+8}\\) is \\((x-3)(x+8)\\). Rewrite the equation with this common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{C(x+8) + D(x-3)}{(x-3)(x+8)} = \\frac{4x-23}{(x-3)(x+8)}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 454,
