  "raw_text": "Step 1: To find the product \\(CD\\), we start by equating the numerators after finding a common denominator on the left side of the equation.\n\nStep 2: The common denominator for \\(\\frac{C}{x-3} + \\frac{D}{x+8}\\) is \\((x-3)(x+8)\\). Rewrite the equation with this common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{C(x+8) + D(x-3)}{(x-3)(x+8)} = \\frac{4x-23}{(x-3)(x+8)}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Since the denominators are equal, we can equate the numerators:\n\n\\[\nC(x+8) + D(x-3) = 4x - 23\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Expand and combine like terms on the left side:\n\n\\[\nCx + 8C + Dx - 3D = 4x - 23\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(C+D)x + (8C - 3D) = 4x - 23\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Equate the coefficients of \\(x\\) and the constant terms from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\nC + D = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n8C - 3D = -23\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Solve the system of linear equations. First, solve for \\(D\\) in terms of \\(C\\) from the first equation:\n\n\\[\nD = 4 - C\n\\]\n\nStep 7: Substitute \\(D = 4 - C\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n8C - 3(4 - C) = -23\n\\]\n\n\\[\n8C - 12 + 3C = -23\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11C - 12 = -23\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11C = -11\n\\]\n\n\\[\nC = -1\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Substitute \\(C = -1\\) back into \\(D = 4 - C\\):\n\n\\[\nD = 4 - (-1) = 5\n\\]\n\nStep 9: Calculate the product \\(CD\\):\n\n\\[\nCD = (-1) \\cdot 5 = -5\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-5}<|im_end|>",
